## ✔️ Summary of Cursor Expectations

Cursor MUST:
- Follow folder structure exactly
- Never mix UI inside features
- Never use client SDK in server logic
- Validate all inputs with Zod
- Use Stripe + Firebase according to architecture
- Follow the provided naming conventions
- Add file headers and JSDoc comments
- Use Server Components by default
- Handle errors gracefully with proper status codes
- Return consistent API response format: `{ success: boolean, data?: any, error?: string }`
- Support responsive design (mobile-first)
- Use DaisyUI components for UI consistency
- Use `getEnv()` helper for environment variable access
- Handle missing Firebase configuration gracefully (boilerplate-friendly)
- Exclude webhooks from CSRF protection
- Return 401 for API routes, redirect for pages when auth required
- Reference `cursor_prompts.md` for common tasks
- Use `overview.md` for documentation (not `README.md` in docs folder)

## 🎯 Production-Tested Patterns

**Reference Implementation:**
- ShipSafe.st is the production-tested reference implementation
- All patterns validated in ThinkMate.online production deployment
- Middleware includes all security improvements from production experience

**Key Production Patterns:**
- Webhook CSRF exclusion (Stripe webhooks use signature verification)
- API route auth differentiation (401 for APIs, redirect for pages)
- CSRF cookie optimization (GET requests only)
- Enhanced security event logging
- Graceful Firebase configuration handling